{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"e18aa801d70bfc1c40193203bd942551e4483914325ada847fb6a9c96d959096","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_a07824e1b2ddcda3387196f6e259485c5339d193ecdfcf0cddfe5a005a49f7e7","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically sound and well-motivated semi-supervised learning framework that effectively leverages context-conditional GANs for image classification. The methodological formulation is clear, and the experimental design is robust, featuring appropriate baselines and ablation studies that validate the contribution of the proposed approach. The authors provide sufficient implementation details and make their code available, supporting reproducibility. The statistical reporting is adequate for the datasets used, with the STL-10 results demonstrating consistent performance across multiple folds.","paper_id":"BJ--gPcxl","paper_identity_sha256":"eefee3fb08dff7ad0ee9258be19f4b450f097823cc51d53a47354103966dd1bf","prompt_identity_sha256":"180997ae84abc1fcfedd74b44da93bcda86531b6bbef41bcecc8b2fc5caef32b","raw_response_sha256":"b43d2cb63f1c8b6e7c8e50fb584781e59fbf49aa742fcf19430d162089c5edf7","request_identity_sha256":"ada01089a047a6eab622922d430e25ded985a8678a2e725bd5abbc29438464fc","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"6fb2824d0bdeecc733a7272f744c73c196d7a311e4a7545b8d29149a0256394f","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The proposed method is well-formulated and mathematically consistent. The authors clearly define the CC-GAN objective and the combined CC-GAN^2 objective, providing a logical progression from standard GANs to the context-conditional variant. The rationale for passing the completed image to the discriminator rather than separate context and patch inputs is explicitly stated to prevent the discriminator from learning to identify discontinuities, which is a sound design choice. The integration of the classification loss with the adversarial loss is clearly defined, and the overall framework is technically coherent without apparent conceptual errors.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The experimental design is comprehensive, utilizing two distinct datasets (STL-10 and PASCAL VOC 2007) to evaluate the method's performance. The choice of baselines is appropriate, including both supervised and semi-supervised methods, as well as a direct comparison to the context-encoder approach. The ablation studies in Table 3 effectively isolate the impact of image resolution, hole size, and low-resolution conditioning, providing clear evidence of the method's robustness. The use of mAP for PASCAL and accuracy for STL-10 aligns with standard evaluation metrics for these tasks.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-029"],"review_text":"The paper provides sufficient detail for reproducibility, including the specific architectures used (VGG-A' for the discriminator and a DCGAN-inspired generator), hyperparameters (learning rate, momentum, and lambda_c), and training procedures. The authors explicitly state that their models and code are available at a public GitHub repository, which significantly enhances the reproducibility of the work. The description of the low-resolution conditioning mechanism is clear, and the training details for both STL-10 and PASCAL experiments are adequately specified.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-007","SRC-008"],"review_text":"The paper thoroughly compares its method against relevant prior work, including the context-encoder approach, CatGAN, and other semi-supervised learning methods. The related work section clearly distinguishes the proposed CC-GAN from existing approaches, highlighting key differences in architecture and loss functions. The experimental comparisons are fair, with the authors acknowledging the larger architecture of their model and providing evidence that the performance gains are due to the method rather than the architecture. The literature review is comprehensive and up-to-date for the time of publication.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-023"],"review_text":"The statistical rigor is appropriate for the datasets used. For STL-10, the authors report the mean and standard deviation across 10 predefined folds, providing a robust measure of performance variability. For PASCAL VOC 2007, the evaluation is conducted on a single test set, which is standard for this dataset. The reported improvements are consistent across different model variants and resolutions, suggesting that the results are not due to chance. The use of multiple folds for STL-10 and the standard test protocol for PASCAL ensure that the statistical validation is sufficient for the claims made.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"44b6822406f9c67fa84ae9bbdb9bc2c26a993a8f013f2928c4b667af734200a0","paper_id":"BJ--gPcxl","paper_ordinal":17,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"b43d2cb63f1c8b6e7c8e50fb584781e59fbf49aa742fcf19430d162089c5edf7","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ--gPcxl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"9bdef41f7ddee5d1fd1d019c6724f3010c724c8569a7fd8cbb51eb2164dba91e","request_identity_sha256":"ada01089a047a6eab622922d430e25ded985a8678a2e725bd5abbc29438464fc","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1060,"prompt_tokens":17483,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18543},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"ada01089a047a6eab622922d430e25ded985a8678a2e725bd5abbc29438464fc","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}